<h1>text</h1>
<p>
(definition)
</p>

<p>
<strong>Definition:</strong>
A list of characters, usually thought of as a list of words separated by spaces.
</p>

<p>
<strong>See also</strong>
<a href="stringMatching.html"><em>string matching</em></a>, <a href="stringMatchwError.html"><em>string matching with errors</em></a>, <a href="longestCommonSubsequence.html"><em>longest common subsequence</em></a>, <a href="invertedIndex.html"><em>inverted index</em></a>.
</p>

<p>
<em>Note:
The term <a href="string.html"><em>string</em></a> usually refers to a small sequence of characters, such as a name or a sentence.  The term text usually refers to a large sequence of characters, such as an article or a book. 
<p> See definition relating to string matching in Algorithms and Theory of Computation Handbook, page 11-26.</em>
</p>

<p>Author: <a href="../Other/contrib.html#authorPEB">PEB</a></p>

